# Netrunner — frontend

Product-only (no platform rename needed when cloning unless the static app path changes).

- Stay vanilla: no React/Vue, no npm, no bundler, no TypeScript transpile step.
- Globals: `NetrunnerGenerators`, `NetrunnerCatalog` (IIFE + `module.exports` for Node unit tests).
- Keep script concerns split (`generators.js` / `catalog.js` / `main.js`). Prefer extending these over new frameworks.
- Load classic `<script defer>` tags from `index.html`. Imprint only needs CSS.
- Version JS/CSS with a shared `?v=` on every HTML reference; **bump `?v=` whenever JS or CSS changes**.
- Card data: `data/catalog.csv` is the editable source; regenerate `data/catalog.json` via `node scripts/csv-to-catalog-json.mjs`.
- Views are query-param driven (`?view=starter-runner`, etc.). No client router framework.
